# 223: the other half of two namespaces (§6 `.42`) — a `fn` and a `let` may
# share a name and both stay reachable. `dup` in value position is the variable;
# `dup(...)` in call position is the function; and `dup(dup)` uses both in one
# expression. An engine with one symbol table would lose whichever came second.
# (A duplicate `fn` name IS a Parse error, but that is a parser case, not this.)
--- source
fn dup(a) { return a * 2; }
let dup = 5;
print dup;
print dup(dup);
print dup(3);
--- expect
5
10
6
